{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/812203-help-trying-to-understand-changeling","id":812203,"title":"Help trying to understand changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-19T16:27:53-08:00","id":812203,"title":"Help trying to understand changeling","content":"I got a copy of The Book and players guide. Theres some concepts im still trying to understand, May ya help me?<br /> <br /> How do changelings work, since They are AWARE OF The mortal World And The dreaming? Do both worlds overlap each other? If GE fights a dog in The mortal World, he will be seen fighting a drag\u00f3n On The dreaming?<br /> Or does this happends as a sort of Split Universe where one Acts while The other is unconcious? <br /> What happend when The mortal dies ?<br /> Do The changelings age at The same time as a Human?<br /> Can you be independant from The courts? <br /> <br /> Sorry for The stupid questions","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T17:33:14-08:00","id":812242,"title":"","content":"1) the dreaming and the mortal world are essentially two planes of existence overlapping. as for the dragon/dog example, sometimes yes, chimera align with a mortal object or animal, but most of the time they are independent and the changeling fighting the dragon looks just like a person waving a stick through the air. it really depends on what's more entertaining for you the player and the group you're playing with. a changeling and mortal selves are both one and the same. it is a faerie soul merged with a human one inhabiting a human body. they will be <br /> <br /> 2)generally speaking when the mortal dies, the fae half reincarnates into another body. the sidhe are an exception in that they don't reincarnate and no one is really sure what happens to them when they die.<br /> <br /> 3)yes. unless they are in the dreaming or a freehold in which case they do not age at all. (i'm pretty sure that's how it works though i could be wrong about the latter)<br /> <br /> 4) Courts are kind of funny in that they are not really political parties in the vein that a vampire sect is. They are in many ways two sides to the changeling's personality mixed with a philosophical dogma. generally speaking Kithian do not operate outside of a court as the court is in their own mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T22:59:27-08:00","id":812400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/812203-help-trying-to-understand-changeling?p=812242#post812242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) Courts are kind of funny in that they are not really political parties in the vein that a vampire sect is. They are in many ways two sides to the changeling's personality mixed with a philosophical dogma. generally speaking Kithian do not operate outside of a court as the court is in their own mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>There <i>was</i> a time when the Courts were political entities on Earth; the Seelie ruled in spring and summer, the Unseelie in autumn and winter. But that was a long time ago, before the Shattering, and when we last checked in, Kithain society was kind of 'default' Seelie. We'll be getting more info on the Courts in both their political and psychological modes in C20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T03:24:58-08:00","id":812480,"title":"","content":"And there's still the Shadow Court, which is a definite political entity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T01:55:17-08:00","id":813251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/812203-help-trying-to-understand-changeling#post812203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got a copy of The Book and players guide. Theres some concepts im still trying to understand, May ya help me?<br /> <br /> How do changelings work, since They are AWARE OF The mortal World And The dreaming? Do both worlds overlap each other? If GE fights a dog in The mortal World, he will be seen fighting a drag\u00f3n On The dreaming?<br /> Or does this happends as a sort of Split Universe where one Acts while The other is unconcious?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm . . . you're familiar with <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b>, right? If so, you can use the Umbra as an analogy.<br /> <br /> Earth and the Near Umbra are divided by the Gauntlet - a spiritual &quot;wall&quot; between the two realities. If a werewolf wants to enter the Near Umbra, or a spirit wants to impact something on Earth, they have to beat the local Gauntlet rating (usually around 7 in most places). Otherwise, the two are completely separate.<br /> <br /> In <i>Changeling</i>, there's no such barrier between Earth and the Dreaming. Chimera (spirits of the Dreaming), changelings, and humans all occupy the exact same plane of reality: breathing the same air, feeling the same sunshine, getting run over by the same car . . . In terms of the Umbral analogy, the Gauntlet is zero.<br /> <br /> The reason humans don't notice all the chimera wandering around (and chimera have a hard time affecting humans) is that the human's Banality acts as a form of spirit gift/armor. Let's call it &quot;Invulnerable to Chimera&quot; - while a chimera might be literally right next to a human, it can't actually touch them without overcoming their Banality. On the bright side, this shields humans from a whole host of dangers. The drawback is that &quot;Invulnerable to Chimera&quot; makes it equally hard to notice any chimerical entities. . . and most humans can't turn it off.<br /> <br /> Beings aware of chimera (changelings, most small kids, and the occasional crazy person) can still directly interact with them - for better or worse. But, if they have to, a changeling can use their Banality to shield themselves from chimera, neutralize chimerically-induces problems (poison, being turned to stone, etc.), or &quot;heal&quot; chimerical damage. The problem is that each time they do so, it becomes harder to turn it &quot;off&quot; next time. Do it too often, and they can become trapped within their Banality, no different than the average human. No faerie magic or powers, no extended lifespan, no ability to see chimera. . . . even their memories (of the Dreaming) are suppressed.<br /> <br /> Note - there are some chimera who (like changelings) have found ways to merge with mundane objects or animals. Regardless of how much Banality a human has, such a chimera can always use their mundane body to interact with them. For example, your dragon/dog example might not be able to use their flaming breath on a human, but they could still bite him (dogs have teeth, after all).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do The changelings age at The same time as a Human? </div> </div> </div>Outside of a freehold (the changeling equivalent of a caern/node/haunt), changelings age like humans. Within a freehold, changelings and enchanted humans don't age at all. And if a changeling choses to wander away from Earth, into the more distant reaches of the Dreaming . . . anything is possible. Growing younger, living a hundred years in a few hours . . .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you be independant from The courts? </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you mean - &quot;court&quot; covers multiple concepts. If you're referring to the governing bodies, then the answer is &quot;yes&quot;. There are plenty of changelings (mostly from the Commoner kiths) who refuse to have anything to do with the various Courts. And even many of those who do, have . . . &quot;interesting&quot; relationships with them (the fae were never noted for being particularly obedient).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, all changelings have both &quot;Seelie&quot; and &quot;Unseelie&quot; parts to their nature. And whichever side they lean to, tends to influence their political sympathies. Barring external factors (such as a feud or corrupt ruler), a Seelie changeling is usually on friendly terms with the various Seelie courts, and hostile towards the Unseelie ones (and vice versa). However, changelings can (and often do) associate with, befriend, or even marry across court lines<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 01-21-2016, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T13:12:48-08:00","id":813591,"title":"","content":"How does The Reencarnation procesos works?<br /> Lets say that Bob is a redcap, he was gubernamentales \u00f1gunned down On An alley and died. What happends to The redcap and how is he reencarnated","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T19:21:33-08:00","id":813834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/812203-help-trying-to-understand-changeling?p=813591#post813591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does The Reencarnation procesos works?<br /> Lets say that Bob is a redcap, he was gubernamentales \u00f1gunned down On An alley and died. What happends to The redcap and how is he reencarnated</div> </div> </div> </div>The human body dies, and the human soul moves on (to Transcendence/Oblivion/etc). The fairy soul, meanwhile, disappears into the Dreaming. It will eventually find an unborn baby with fairy blood (often related to its previous incarnation), and the two fuse into a new changeling. So Bob the Redcap becomes Gina the Redcap, Gina will eventually become Ricardo the Redcap, Ricardo becomes Ivana . . .<br /> <br /> Despite it being the same fairy soul, though, the new changeling is very much a new entity. If Bob dies at fifty, and Gina awakens at six, Gina will look/talk/act like a girl in kindergarten - not a middle aged man. Even though the Redcap soul hasn't changed (and is possibly thousands of years old), the human half is dominant.<br /> <br /> If you need a pop culture example, you <i>might</i> look at the Doctor (in <i>Doctor Who</i>). Each time he regenerates, its still technically the Doctor . . . but the old personality/beliefs/quirks die with the previous incarnation. Its just that the Doctor can create a brand new (adult) body, while the fairy soul has to go find a new infant one, somewhere out in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T05:17:11-08:00","id":814055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/812203-help-trying-to-understand-changeling?p=813834#post813834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The human body dies, and the human soul moves on (to Transcendence/Oblivion/etc). The fairy soul, meanwhile, disappears into the Dreaming. It will eventually find an unborn baby with fairy blood (often related to its previous incarnation), and the two fuse into a new changeling. So Bob the Redcap becomes Gina the Redcap, Gina will eventually become Ricardo the Redcap, Ricardo becomes Ivana . . .<br /> <br /> Despite it being the same fairy soul, though, the new changeling is very much a new entity. If Bob dies at fifty, and Gina awakens at six, Gina will look/talk/act like a girl in kindergarten - not a middle aged man. Even though the Redcap soul hasn't changed (and is possibly thousands of years old), the human half is dominant.<br /> <br /> If you need a pop culture example, you <i>might</i> look at the Doctor (in <i>Doctor Who</i>). Each time he regenerates, its still technically the Doctor . . . but the old personality/beliefs/quirks die with the previous incarnation. Its just that the Doctor can create a brand new (adult) body, while the fairy soul has to go find a new infant one, somewhere out in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>System wise, do They keep their cantrips or They Must start from Zero?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T06:40:35-08:00","id":814087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/812203-help-trying-to-understand-changeling?p=814055#post814055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> System wise, do They keep their cantrips or They Must start from Zero?</div> </div> </div> </div>System-wise, they start from zero. And they also are reborn as babies, so unless the game has a multi-year hiatus to let the new Changeling grow up enough to be even vaguely playable and undergo Chrysalis, the character isn't coming back to the same game via this route. (At least not without some plot-relevant age-up plot contrivance.) If, for some reason, the character DID &quot;come back&quot; this way in the same game, the ST could reasonably require a high level of Past Lives background and then grant XP to catch the PC up, though, on the grounds that the Childling has retained just that much of his previous life's memories and skills. But that would be ST generosity; by the rules, a new PC is a new PC, and a reincarnation is a new PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T11:08:45-08:00","id":814279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/812203-help-trying-to-understand-changeling?p=813251#post813251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, if they have to, a changeling can use their Banality to shield themselves from chimera, neutralize chimerically-induces problems (poison, being turned to stone, etc.), or &amp;quot;heal&amp;quot; chimerical damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Heal' probably isn't the right word. They can ignore their injuries for a turn and take a point of Banality, but the wounds will still affect them when they stop ignoring them. Ignoring them for more than a few turns is a sure way to increase your permanent Banality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T10:50:15-08:00","id":814922,"title":"","content":"A way to look at Changeling reincarnation might to through the lens of Fallen 'reincarnation', and how they differ. At the core they are the same idea: the soul finds a new body and inhabits it. The differences are:<br /> -Demons look for 'soulless*' bodies, while Changelings look for unborn bodies. This means that Changelings take at least 9 months longer to come back.<br /> -For Fallen their soul is the dominant one, for Changelings the 'dominant' soul is their mortal one. This means that a reincarnated Demon is the same character, but with some tweaked stats (probably abilities, mostly knowledges), whereas a Changeling is a new character and probably functionally 'mortal' until their fae soul awakens.<br /> -Demons have a limited range for a new body, Changelings don't. Demon's reincarnation is essentially a 'last chance' mechanic allowing characters to try and get a new body, Changeling's is a setting element.<br /> <br /> Waiting for my copy of 2e to arrive, so I can't really help with any of the other questions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *oh boy, how this is treated is a problem, and although in many cases pushing the soul out that tiny bit is easy, Demons objectively steal bodies, while with Changelings it's more complex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}